#N canvas 20 20 4900 3970 12;
#X declare -path ../Cut\ It;
#X text 20 20 phase5-bench -- the Phase 5 acceptance run: clock \, transport \, the map and the LED. Ten seconds a step \, so you can watch the OLED and the aux button and mark each one off. Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch: it only pushes onto tempo \, param \, start \, stop and panic \, exactly as a controller would., f 110;
#X text 20 110 RUN IN THE FOREGROUND. Every step prints what it is sending and a PASS IF line -- including the steps whose correct result is that NOTHING happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark. Steps 1 to 11 drive themselves and 12 to 13 need your hands on the Organelle itself., f 110;
#X text 20 200 IT FINDS c_clock ITSELF \, through the declare above -- so opening this file straight from Pd's File menu works and no -path is needed. If the console ever says c_clock ... couldn't create \, the two counts below will read 0 and mean nothing. A c_clock created after the patch is already running is fine: it seeds its own tempo., f 110;
#X text 20 290 STEP 1 RE-ASSERTS THE DEFAULTS -- 120 BPM and stopped -- so the run is repeatable without reopening the patch. Everything after it builds on that. NO COMMAS OR SEMICOLONS IN A PASS IF LINE: both are message separators \, so one comma splits the string and the remainder lands somewhere unhelpful., f 110;
#X obj 4200 260 r \$0-say;
#X obj 4200 300 print;
#X obj 700 420 r clock;
#X obj 700 460 t b;
#X obj 700 500 f;
#X obj 700 540 + 1;
#X obj 840 580 t f f;
#X obj 840 650 f;
#X obj 1040 460 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 1040 500 0;
#X obj 1040 560 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 1040 600 0;
#X obj 700 650 r \$0-read;
#X obj 840 710 print M-BEATS;
#X obj 1700 340 c_clock 1 4;
#X obj 1700 460 t b;
#X obj 1700 500 f;
#X obj 1700 540 + 1;
#X obj 1840 580 t f f;
#X obj 1840 650 f;
#X obj 2040 460 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 2040 500 0;
#X obj 2040 560 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 2040 600 0;
#X obj 1700 650 r \$0-read;
#X obj 1840 710 print C1-BEATS-ratio-1;
#X obj 2700 340 c_clock 1.5 4;
#X obj 2700 460 t b;
#X obj 2700 500 f;
#X obj 2700 540 + 1;
#X obj 2840 580 t f f;
#X obj 2840 650 f;
#X obj 3040 460 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 3040 500 0;
#X obj 3040 560 r \$0-zero;
#X msg 3040 600 0;
#X obj 2700 650 r \$0-read;
#X obj 2840 710 print C2-BEATS-ratio-1.5;
#X text 700 800 THE TWO c_clock INSTANCES ARE WHAT STEPS 2 AND 3 EXIST FOR. Ratio 1 must land on exactly the same beats as the master reference and ratio 1.5 must produce half again as many -- under real DSP on the real device \, which is the one thing the Mac cannot prove. The deployed patch instantiates neither \, because nothing consumes a beat yet., f 100;
#X obj 140 1500 del 6000;
#X obj 240 1528 t b b b b;
#X msg 320 1566 === STEP-01-of-15 === baseline -- re-asserting 120 BPM and stopped;
#X obj 320 1596 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1566 PASS IF: two bars with a small gate mark under each and 120-bpm in the footer -- and the aux button lit DARK BLUE. This step exists so the run repeats without reopening the patch;
#X obj 1100 1596 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 1566 120;
#X obj 2700 1596 s tempo;
#X msg 3200 1566 bang;
#X obj 3200 1596 s stop;
#X obj 20 1400 loadbang;
#X obj 140 1650 del 10000;
#X obj 240 1678 t b b b;
#X msg 320 1716 === STEP-02-of-15 === COUNTING -- zeroing the beat counters for 10 s at 120 BPM;
#X obj 320 1746 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1716 PASS IF: NOTHING VISIBLE CHANGES. The transport is still stopped and the clock is running anyway -- which is exactly what is being counted;
#X obj 1100 1746 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 1716 bang;
#X obj 2700 1746 s \$0-zero;
#X obj 140 1800 del 10000;
#X obj 240 1828 t b b b;
#X msg 320 1866 === STEP-03-of-15 === READ THE COUNTS -- the clock ran for 10 s while STOPPED;
#X obj 320 1896 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 1866 PASS IF: M-BEATS 20 or 21 -- C1-BEATS the same number -- C2-BEATS 30 or 31. A zero anywhere means the clock does not run until the transport does -- or on the Mac it means DSP is off which looks exactly the same;
#X obj 1100 1896 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 1866 bang;
#X obj 2700 1896 s \$0-read;
#X obj 140 1950 del 10000;
#X obj 240 1978 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2016 === STEP-04-of-15 === START THE TRANSPORT;
#X obj 320 2046 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2016 PASS IF: the aux button turns GREEN and the 404 starts its pattern. WATCH EXT ON THE 404'S PATTERN SELECT SCREEN -- the number beside a pad is that SAMPLE's BPM and never moves;
#X obj 1100 2046 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2016 bang;
#X obj 2700 2046 s start;
#X obj 140 2100 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2128 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2166 === STEP-05-of-15 === TEMPO THROUGH THE MAP -- og-knob-1 at 0;
#X obj 320 2196 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2166 PASS IF: the footer reads 10-bpm and the 404's EXT number slides down to meet it within a second or two. THIS IS THE REAL done-when;
#X obj 1100 2196 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2166 og-knob-1 0;
#X obj 2700 2196 s param;
#X obj 140 2250 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2278 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2316 === STEP-06-of-15 === TEMPO THROUGH THE MAP -- og-knob-1 at 1;
#X obj 320 2346 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2316 PASS IF: the footer reads 500-bpm and the 404's EXT slides up again. A slide rather than a snap IS the inference working -- it snaps only to a tempo it has already learned;
#X obj 1100 2346 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2316 og-knob-1 1;
#X obj 2700 2346 s param;
#X obj 140 2400 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2428 t b b b b;
#X msg 320 2466 === STEP-07-of-15 === OUT OF RANGE -- 5000 sent TWICE;
#X obj 320 2496 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2466 PASS IF: the footer reads 600-bpm and EXACTLY ONE alert appears -- a bordered box naming u_tempo. The second 5000 must be silent because the VALUE did not change;
#X obj 1100 2496 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2466 5000;
#X obj 2700 2496 s tempo;
#X msg 3200 2466 5000;
#X obj 3200 2496 s tempo;
#X obj 140 2550 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2578 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2616 === STEP-08-of-15 === OUT OF RANGE THE OTHER WAY -- 0;
#X obj 320 2646 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2616 PASS IF: the footer reads 5-bpm and a SECOND alert appears. The verdict did not change but the value did -- and this is the case that was broken once;
#X obj 1100 2646 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2616 0;
#X obj 2700 2646 s tempo;
#X obj 140 2700 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2728 t b b b;
#X msg 320 2766 === STEP-09-of-15 === BACK TO 120;
#X obj 320 2796 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2766 PASS IF: the footer reads 120-bpm and NO alert appears at all;
#X obj 1100 2796 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2766 120;
#X obj 2700 2796 s tempo;
#X obj 140 2850 del 10000;
#X obj 240 2878 t b b b b;
#X msg 320 2916 === STEP-10-of-15 === STOP -- and the clock must NOT stop with it;
#X obj 320 2946 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 2916 PASS IF: the aux button goes DARK BLUE and the 404 stops -- but its display MUST STILL SAY EXT. If it falls back to BPM the clock stopped with the transport and that is the bug this step exists for;
#X obj 1100 2946 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 2916 bang;
#X obj 2700 2946 s \$0-zero;
#X msg 3200 2916 bang;
#X obj 3200 2946 s stop;
#X obj 140 3000 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3028 t b b b;
#X msg 320 3066 === STEP-11-of-15 === READ THE COUNTS WHILE STOPPED;
#X obj 320 3096 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3066 PASS IF: M-BEATS 20 or 21 again. Stop the pulse stream and the 404 stretches every sample to a stale tempo -- so this is the least obvious requirement in the phase;
#X obj 1100 3096 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 3066 bang;
#X obj 2700 3096 s \$0-read;
#X obj 140 3150 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3178 t b b b;
#X msg 320 3216 === STEP-12-of-15 === PANIC;
#X obj 320 3246 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3216 PASS IF: the aux button turns RED and the footer says panic -- and the clock is STILL running underneath;
#X obj 1100 3246 s \$0-say;
#X msg 2700 3216 bang;
#X obj 2700 3246 s panic;
#X obj 140 3300 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3328 t b b;
#X msg 320 3366 === STEP-13-of-15 === BY HAND -- press the aux button twice;
#X obj 320 3396 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3366 PASS IF: ON THE DEVICE use the real button. ON THE MAC use aux-tap and NOT the aux toggle -- aux is momentary 1 then 0 and only the 1 is a press \, so a toggle needs two clicks per press and the uncheck is meant to do nothing. First press GREEN and the 404 starts \, second DARK BLUE and it stops. If nothing happens at all then mother is eating the press;
#X obj 1100 3396 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 3450 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3478 t b b;
#X msg 320 3516 === STEP-14-of-15 === BY HAND -- sweep KNOB 1 all the way and back;
#X obj 320 3546 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3516 PASS IF: og-knob-1 appears as a parameter row on the OLED and the footer tracks between 10-bpm and 500-bpm. The 404 follows the sweep;
#X obj 1100 3546 s \$0-say;
#X obj 140 3600 del 10000;
#X obj 240 3628 t b b;
#X msg 320 3666 === STEP-15-of-15 === done -- press Ctrl-C;
#X obj 320 3696 s \$0-say;
#X msg 1100 3666 PASS IF: every step above was marked off. If 2 3 10 or 11 failed the clock is wrong -- if 5 6 or 14 failed the map is -- if 4 12 or 13 failed the transport or the LED is;
#X obj 1100 3696 s \$0-say;
#X connect 4 0 5 0;
